{"duration_api_ms":225641,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"1e7411ac-be2b-43fd-97a1-ff70e2728bf9","total_cost_usd":0.269048,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12366,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":21958,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16062},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":21958,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":21958,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12366,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.269048,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":16062,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front has one point, C-05ff421c45e2 (279k W/m2, 394.04 K). The normalised hypervolume of 0.331 matches that point exactly. The temperature axis dominates the score, because 1 K is worth roughly 15 times more than 10k W/m2. The feasible region is a narrow cluster near D 3.0-3.37 m, bluntness 1.0-1.25, cone 66-70 deg and gamma -3.1 to -3.6 deg. Three constraints bound it. max_g <= 12 sets a steepest gamma of about -3.58 deg. Heatshield mass fraction caps D at about 3.38 m at high bluntness and cone angle. Geometry validity caps bluntness at about 0.4/cos(cone)+0.1, which is 1.27 at 70 deg. Steeper gamma, larger D and higher bluntness all lower both objectives, so the best remaining move is to push toward the corner where all three limits meet.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-3583b7488cf2 (D3.3, bl1.2, c70, gamma -3.6) has the lowest temperature of any near-feasible candidate at 392.29 K and 285.6k, but g=12.016 fails the limit by 0.1%. C-dcc8aaeb364a (gamma -3.55) gives g=11.921, so the g limit sits near gamma -3.58 to -3.59.\",\"C-05ff421c45e2 (D3.35, bl1.1) has mass margin 0.0179. C-0d18a7fb8799 (D3.3, bl1.15) has 0.048, C-15107d6a0298 (D3.2, bl1.2) has 0.106 and C-613443d901da (D3.0069) has 0.209. Margin falls about 0.6 per metre of D, so D is capped near 3.37-3.38.\",\"C-3a694f0320f1 and C-dcc8aaeb364a differ only in gamma (-3.4 vs -3.55). Mass margin is identical at 0.04787, so mass fraction does not depend on gamma. Temperature falls about 1.1 K per 0.1 deg of steeper gamma. Flux rises only about 2.8k per 0.1 deg.\",\"Geometry failures such as C-892b8b20e709 and C-a91d9ef63c92 fit an axial cone length of (0.4 + 0.1cos(theta) - bl*cos(theta))*D / tan(theta). I checked this against the failure messages (-369 vs -367 mm, -2983 vs -2984 mm). bl=1.24 at cone 70 is valid, with a positive length of about 12 mm.\",\"Flux falls with bluntness and D. C-3583b7488cf2 (bl1.2, D3.3) and C-0d18a7fb8799 (bl1.15) show about -3k per +0.05 bl. C-05ff421c45e2 (D3.35) has the lowest flux at 279k.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak deceleration in a ballistic entry is roughly independent of ballistic coefficient, so max_g is set mainly by gamma (my prior knowledge, consistent with the g values in the table). That makes about -3.58 deg the steepest allowed entry. Steeper entry shortens the heat pulse and lowers bondline temperature. A larger diameter lowers ballistic coefficient and raises the nose radius, which cuts flux and temperature, but heatshield mass fraction limits D. Higher bluntness and cone angle reduce flux and slightly help mass margin. The best corner is therefore D about 3.30-3.37, bluntness 1.24-1.25, cone 70 deg and gamma about -3.55 to -3.58. I also add a few shallow-gamma, low-flux points to spread the front along the flux axis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The g-limit is close to the gamma range I probe, so several proposals with gamma between -3.55 and -3.585 could fail max_g by 0.1-0.5%. Mass margin at D 3.36-3.37 is predicted to be only about 0.01 and could turn negative. My sensitivities are rough finite differences from confounded rows. The geometry-validity rule is fitted to only two failures, and bl 1.25 at cone 70 leaves only about 8 mm of fore-cone length. Predicted temperature gains are small (1-3 K).\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Raise bluntness to 1.24 and steepen gamma to -3.5 at D3.35. This should lower both flux and temperature while staying well inside the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safe step that should dominate the current single front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Same corner with gamma -3.55, trading a little g margin for lower temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the mid-range of the gamma trade at max D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to -3.58 at D3.35 and bl1.24, close to the g limit, for minimum temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary near the best corner; predicted g is about 11.97-12.0.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D (3.36) with bl1.24 and gamma -3.56. This uses the last bit of mass margin to cut temperature and flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Candidate for the best overall corner; mass margin should be about 0.015.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"D3.37, bl1.24, gamma -3.52. This probes the maximum diameter for lowest flux while staying inside the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.52},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the mass margin (about 0.009) still holds at D3.37.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3583b7488cf2\",\"rationale\":\"Take the near-feasible D3.3 point and raise bl to 1.24. Backing gamma off to -3.58 should bring g just under 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Converts the g-infeasible C-3583b7488cf2 into a feasible near-best point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3583b7488cf2\",\"rationale\":\"D3.3, bl1.24, gamma -3.55, giving more g margin than the previous proposal.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Robust feasible point around the corner with a comfortable mass margin of about 0.05.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3583b7488cf2\",\"rationale\":\"D3.3, bl1.24, gamma -3.5: the flux-leaning side of the front at this D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills in the gamma sweep at D3.3 to build front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3583b7488cf2\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate D3.32 with bl1.24 and gamma -3.57.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.32,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests a compromise between the D3.3 and D3.35 clusters.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-15107d6a0298\",\"rationale\":\"D3.25 has ample mass margin, about 0.09. The steeper gamma of -3.57 is allowed because g is lower at smaller D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the D vs gamma trade at lower D, where g is slightly lower.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-15107d6a0298\",\"rationale\":\"D3.2 at the steepest gamma -3.6, with bl1.24. This tests whether smaller D lets us exceed -3.58.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":296800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Calibrates the g dependence on D at the limit of gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Low-flux end of the front: D3.36, bl1.24, shallow gamma -3.3. Flux should fall well below 279k at some cost in temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front along the flux axis so the trade-off is well covered.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Extreme low-flux probe: D3.37, bl1.24, gamma -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks how far flux can be pushed down along the shallow-gamma branch.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0d18a7fb8799\",\"rationale\":\"D3.3, bl1.24, gamma -3.3: a low-flux point with more mass margin than the D3.36 variant.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Provides a safe low-flux front candidate.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Test cone 69 with bl1.2 at D3.34 and gamma -3.55 to check cone sensitivity of flux, temperature and mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks that the cone-angle effect is small so the cone can stay at 70.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-030a1a891b31\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 68 with bl1.12 at D3.3 and gamma -3.55. This is a lower-cone variant, valid since bl < 1.168 at 68 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.12,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Diversifies the cone angle while remaining near the feasible cluster.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3583b7488cf2\",\"rationale\":\"D3.28, bl1.25, gamma -3.585. This pushes toward the g limit with slightly reduced D to hold g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.28,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.585},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests both the g boundary and bl1.25 geometry validity, with about 8 mm of fore-cone length.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3583b7488cf2\",\"rationale\":\"D3.31, bl1.25, gamma -3.56 in the middle of the promising corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.31,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the additional benefit of bl1.25 over 1.24 and whether geometry stays valid.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"D3.34, bl1.25, gamma -3.53 at high D and bluntness with moderate g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the flux-favouring side of the corner near the mass limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05ff421c45e2\",\"rationale\":\"Lower bluntness (1.0) at D3.35 and gamma -3.55 to measure the bluntness sensitivity of flux, temperature and mass margin at fixed D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the bluntness effect to refine the surrogate for later rounds.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":179399,"type":"result","duration_ms":225717,"uuid":"85c70c71-58c2-473e-ae20-a0635a5e4a67","ttft_stream_ms":1763,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":1764,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
